Subject: Cantor Coordination Transport Measurement P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 089308ec-b50e-4e0d-b2ba-022b6f7c8796
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Coordination_Transport_Measurement_P0.sop

& [Need] is evidence before stateful optimization
  + the stateless tool maximizes inspectability restart simplicity and deterministic replay but repeats admitted context
  + a registry could reduce repeated bytes but would create hidden custody concurrency recovery and authentication surfaces
  + exact production JSON accounting can distinguish context repetition schema size and growing dynamic checkpoints before selecting that tradeoff

& [Method] is deterministic rather than timing-sensitive
  + byte measurement is stable across machine load and requires no benchmark clock
  + several quotas expose the host-call tradeoff directly
  + one checked fixture supports architectural direction without pretending to establish general performance

& [Safety] retains current behavior
  + the measurement calls only pure admission and coordination functions
  + no server provider model or external effect is involved
  + a zero-byte handle ceiling is explicitly more optimistic than any implementable registry

& [Conclusion] is measure exact structured payloads before governing a context registry

